cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: own-baseline
abstract: >-
  A single-cell potency or stemness score is usually validated by correlating it
  against a pseudotime, a marker panel, or a known hierarchy. A score that
  restates sequencing depth passes that test, and so does a score carrying real
  ordering information. This package implements the check that separates them:
  residualize the score on the low-order statistic its own authors say it
  approximates, and ask whether what is left still orders cells, judged against
  a null-calibrated floor computed at that value's own n and its own
  score-primitive rank correlation.
type: software
authors:
